Declare rules_distroless's apt hub and filemap repos reproducible so they can use the
repo contents cache.

`translate_dependency_set` (the apt hub) is a pure function of `lock_content`,
`depset_name`, `mergedusr` and the `package_template` file, which is a recorded input.
`deb_filemap` only writes its `files` attribute to disk. Without this both rerun on every
CI runner, and reading `package_template` materialises all of `@rules_distroless`.

Not yet raised upstream.

diff --git a/apt/private/deb_filemap.bzl b/apt/private/deb_filemap.bzl
index f8f50ae..326f2b0 100644
--- a/apt/private/deb_filemap.bzl
+++ b/apt/private/deb_filemap.bzl
@@ -10,6 +10,12 @@
     rctx.file("filemap.json", rctx.attr.files)
     rctx.file("BUILD.bazel", 'exports_files(["filemap.json"], visibility = ["//visibility:public"])\n')
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks rctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(rctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return rctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 deb_filemap = repository_rule(
     implementation = _deb_filemap_impl,
     attrs = {
